# great-pm Project

> Copy this file to `.great-pm/PROJECT.md` in your project root and customize.
> Every great-pm agent reads this file at the start of its work.

## Project

product: <your product name>
archetype: <b2b-saas | consumer-app | marketplace | dev-tool | platform | mobile-app | ecommerce>
ai_pm_pack: <true | false>   # true activates the AI-PM overlay pack for AI products
project_size: <small | medium | large>

## Phase

phase: <discovery | building | launched | scaling>
loop_stage: <discover | strategize | prioritize | define | launch | measure>

## Team

team-size: 1
mode: <solo | small-team | growing>
approval-level: <verbose | expert | gates-only | auto>

## Gate policy

> Controls whether agents may auto-close gates or whether a human must
> run /pm-gate approve <id> explicitly. great-pm's default is `explicit`
> (more conservative than engineering's `auto`) because PM gates have
> larger blast radius than engineering ones.

gate-policy: explicit  # explicit | auto

## Goals

- <primary product goal — what would success look like in 6 months?>
- <secondary goal>
- <stretch / north-star aspiration>

## Active initiatives (running in parallel)

> great-pm supports multiple initiatives at once. List each with its current
> loop stage. Unrelated work never blocks unrelated work; only same-initiative
> dependencies gate.

- <initiative-slug-1>: stage=<discover|strategize|...>, lead-agent=<name>
- <initiative-slug-2>: stage=<...>, lead-agent=<...>

## Context

<Anything project-specific the agents should know: market position, hard
constraints, regulatory scope, team strengths, technical posture, things
that have already been tried. The richer this section, the better the
agent output.>

## Compliance & risk (if applicable)

compliance: []  # e.g. [gdpr, hipaa, pci-dss-saq-a]
risk: <low | medium | high>

## Memory & query rule

> Before reading source files, agents query memory layers in this order:
> 1. `.great-pm/lessons.md` — project-specific lessons learned
> 2. `~/.great-pm/decisions.md` — global cross-project decisions
> 3. `.great-pm/verdicts/` — past agent verdicts (DONE / BLOCKED with rationale)
> 4. Only then read source files / current state for the actual work

## Notes

> This file is yours. Edit freely. Agents read it; they do not overwrite it.
